From 9e6ab3e10d63fdb4c3d1e58d43619a623beea4fe
Subject: chore(bevy-explorer): fix the build warnings the 1.99 toolchain raises (#368)
Origin: https://github.com/decentraland/dcl-one/commit/9e6ab3e10d63fdb4c3d1e58d43619a623beea4fe
Date: 2026-11-09T15:26:59+01:00

Rust 1.99.1 raises warnings in the vendored Bevy fork, the Explorer tests and the vendored ENet crate. This PR fixes each warning at its site and keeps the behaviour the same.

ComponentCloneBehavior gets a manual PartialEq that compares Custom function pointers with fn_addr_eq. The derived implementation compared the pointers directly.
WorldId::new calls try_update on targets with pointer-sized atomics and keeps fetch_update for the portable_atomic fallback (upstream #26020). try_update needs Rust 1.95, so bevy, bevy_ecs and bevy_input_focus declare rust-version = "1.95.0".
Bevy loses unused imports, the unused UiScale parameter of set_camera_window_cursor_position, redundant alloc:: paths and the parentheses around dyn Any + Send. The avatar and scene runner tests lose unused prelude::* imports.
ENet patch 0007 names the borrowed Event<'_, C> lifetime in the connected host's handle_event, check_events and service. The lock file and the checksums record the patch.
docs/guidelines/bevy-fork.md records the WorldId change, the 1.95 floor and the toolchain pins. It also states the rule: fix a warning the pinned toolchain raises at its site.
